TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"transient","diagnosis":"Failed during lane admission before any worktree, worker, or gate execution occurred, so nothing about the task's content was exercised. The failure record carries stage \"lane\", verdict \"flow-error\", a null exit code, empty stderr, and detail {\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}} with no populated details payload. Corroborating evidence: gateOutputs is empty, workerOutcomeClaim is null, previousWorkerOutcomes is empty, and the diff block reports available=false with reason \"task failed before a worktree was prepared\" and a null head against the all-zero base revision. There is therefore no failing check id and no offending path to cite, because no acceptance criterion ran; the sole criterion rdma-package-sound was never invoked. The task definition itself shows no admission-blocking defect: it declares no dependencies, its conflictDomains [\"host/rdma\",\"tests\"] cover every path its goal directs it to write (host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh, host/rdma/attended-bringup.md, host/rdma/ab-protocol.md, and the tests suite extension), and its read-only references to specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6, specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md, specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-hardening-addendum.md, and scripts/stage-weights.sh require no write authority outside those domains. The worker envelope did not request authority, so the always-blocked needs-authority path does not apply. That leaves an orchestration-side admission refusal — the flow machinery declining to open the lane at ordinal 4 — rather than an actionable in-task fix or an out-of-task authority, dependency, or gate-contract defect. Re-dispatch of the identical task revision sha256:b322b54d6da9831c25a2e55569a9a8ce4c293840285b6225b2760d2c20ee9460 against a healthy lane is the correct next action; it should consume the bounded machinery-retry budget and not the task's two-attempt cap. If admission is denied again with the same code and an empty details payload, escalate to the operator as a flow-layer fault rather than re-diagnosing the task, since no repository change under host/rdma or tests could alter this outcome."}
